ry time i got  one on offense and try to make a big  play and i felt like i was doing that  most of training camp  and then with the 101s and everything um  showing them i can block catch and  everything like that and i feel like  everything that i did just kind of  opened their eyes a little bit and then  it was kind of okay maybe this guy can  play and then  start rolling with the ones and i'm not  sure what their conversation was but  sure they were good  you you obviously impressed them i mean  there's no doubt about that i just as  you as a rookie like could you tell that  maybe  there was they had fallen out of love  with leonard fournette like how shocked  were you when they actually cut him did  you see it coming at all  uh no i don't think anyone saw it coming  we were kind of just all just chilling  in um rooms waiting for meetings and  everything and then we found out but uh  yeah it just kind of was kind of  surprising because i mean he was  practicing with us and  as a rookie you don't really  know how things like that go you don't  think uh the guy's only really  practicing and then just gets gets cut  a guy like that gets cut but i mean  i think  we couldn't really tell what was going  on he was in practice he was just  learning from that i mean just  practicing well doing everything he can  so  this was surprising though  mike mike i i'm gonna ask one more just  real quick i'm always interested with  like the small school guys you didn't  get drafted i don't know how the hell  that didn't happen illinois state people  like oh can this guy play in the nfl  what's gonna happen when he gets in  there  i want two things  what was tougher about the nfl than you  expected what was easier about the nfl  than you expected don't be bashful now  come on give us the truth  um  a tough thing was  probably the speed for me  um i mean coming out i didn't have a  good 40 but uh  i say with the speed and then i think  the easiest thing was just for me it was  picking up the offense uh i studied it  along like before i got to jacksonville  i was just studying the whole playbook  and i kind of caught on to it pretty  well  so i think those two were  main things  james how much motivation did you take  from the fact that you weren't drafted  did that help give you the kick that you  needed to go into camp and and impress  the coaching staff the way you did  um yeah uh  i wouldn't say that motivated me it was  just more of towards the end of the  draft when i knew it probably wasn't  gonna happen i just i was just like  just getting me on the team and once i  got on the team and once i got there  it's just playing football and there's  no time to sit back and relax at all and  i had to open their eyes somehow and  that was my mindset just going in  most impressive  freakiest guy you saw on a field this  year in your match you can't pick your  own team nobody on your no none of your  buddies but just the guy that you were  sitting on the sideline or playing  against where you just went whoa i had  no idea this guy was like this  um  i would say his product it was pretty  cool watching uh aaron rodgers play when  we went to green bay  that was pretty cool see i knew i liked  you uh we were i knew we were eye to eye  on something there see aaron rodgers  that was easy one yep i knew i liked  this guy mike he's smart he knows  football  well i don't know  he's like  he's the president of the aaron rodgers  fan club so uh yeah he likes anybody  that comes on the show and says they  like aaron rodgers hey how do you like  urban meyer because you got a new coach  i don't know if you've spoken to him yet  or what the buzz is around the the  players but what's your thought on the  guy who's going to be taking over the  team starting this year  um  i'll talk with him a few times uh he was  he seems pretty cool  excited to get to work with all of us  and um  yeah i think all of us are just excited  to have him and  see what he brings  to pra